  "body": "Consider the following test:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nu = new URL(\"https://github.com/whatwg/url/issues/new\");\r\nu.protocol = \"ht\\ntp\";\r\nu.href\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn Chrome, Firefox, and Safari, `u.href` retains the original `https` protocol. This behavior as it relates to the Location object is in fact tested by WPT(!): search for `\\x0A` in [html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-protocol-setter.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-protocol-setter.html#L48).",
